From eabf062c5c77df140bd51a4d92f8294bfcefb96c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 12:31:13 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Add explicit nonblocking POSIX TCP streams for V2 transport

Implement numeric IPv4/IPv6 endpoints, move-only single-descriptor stream and listener ownership, fixed injected connect deadlines, one-fd zero-timeout readiness, and single-attempt nonblocking I/O and accept. Refused creation preserves existing connections and failed accept preserves outputs. Configure close-on-exec and per-socket/send SIGPIPE suppression before publication; close once without ambiguous EINTR retries.

Keep Linux/macOS platform scope explicit, with no DNS, default endpoints, seeds, network profile adoption or node activation. The existing Transport borrows stable stream objects; caller bounds connection counts and scheduler calls while kernel and transport buffers retain separate quotas.

Actual macOS arm64 IPv4/IPv6 localhost ephemeral-port checks pass: Debug 1/1 in 0.46s and ASan+UBSan 1/1 in 0.40s. Cover reads/writes/EOF, fixed deadlines, backpressure, EPIPE survival, failure-preserved outputs, fd moves/reuse, and fragmented existing Transport handshake/application bytes. Independent read-only review found no concrete blocker. Only five new adapter/test files; Linux execution and shared build integration remain separate.
